  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, singleprofile, PCA n2000) achieves 0.485 acc / 0.464 F1, while config_010 (Image, singleprofile, ResNet50) achieves only 0.208 acc / 0.172 F1. RNA is clearly the dominant modality, and the multiprofile/aggregation axis is entirely untested. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with simple avgpool aggregation improve the RNA representation, holding the encoder (PCA n2000) constant? This isolates the profile+aggregation effect as a single-axis change from our best baseline. Why this is the best next experiment: With only two completed runs, the most informative next step is to determine whether multiprofile aggregation can push the already-best modality higher. The answer directly gates whether the many multiprofile multimodal configurations (config_018–051) are worth pursuing, and it keeps the comparison clean by changing only profile setting and aggregation relative to config_001. Avgpool is chosen over transformer as the simpler, more interpretable first test of aggregation."
}

